			<div class="content" id="post-content-3602876">
									

<p>The excerpt in the first audio log actually breaks the immersion for me&#8212;sure, it's competently written, but for someone to read aloud a sample of known info/cognito hazard? I found it really hard to believe. And wouldn't it considered a breach if it's read from a written object? Or if it's purely from memory, I feel it'd be really redundant for the memorizer of the document to remember a sample of the anomaly, especially one that's that long.</p>
<p>And we do know that information tend to mutate within a telephone game, which this document basically is, so the Foundation should've at least speculated that the second Audio Log could happen.</p>
<p>Novoting.</p>

